# Dog physics

Fourth species. Sibling of `Human`, `Bird`, `PlantTree`. Do not derive
`Dog` from `Human`. Reuse `HumanSegment`, `Muscle`, `JointFriction`.

Play: scene `Dog`, `dogCount = 1`. All other scenes: `dogCount = 0`.
Headless: `-dog 1` on flat ground. The human stand does not spawn dogs
unless `-dog` is set.

Signs review (no `Dog.cs` yet): `Trials/Runs/dog_physics_signs.md`.

## Body

Sagittal, faces +X. Chest cranial (+X), pelvis caudal (−X). Digitigrade
paws (small foot, high ankle). No second toe segment.

| Part | Segments |
|---|---|
| Trunk | `Chest` (vestibular), `Pelvis`, lumbar hinge |
| Head | `Neck`, `Head` — cranial face of Chest, not stacked on the withers |
| Jaw | `Jaw` on the head (TMJ). Closed `0`, open plus. Trigger + `JawStrike` |
| Tail | five vertebrae (`Tail`…`Tail5`), friction + rest spring; muscles only on the first |
| Front L/R | upper, forearm, paw |
| Rear L/R | thigh, shin, paw |

Left/right pair: visual offset on `Visual` only. Do not put
`hipHalfSpacing` / shoulder spacing into X anchors (that is a lunge).
Front vs rear **are** separated in X — that is body length, not a lunge.
Play gizmos: Unity's green `BoxCollider2D` box is on the body, so a
pair looks like one column. The far sprite is not missing a collider —
`HumanSegment.OnDrawGizmos` draws a cyan wire on `Visual` only. Do not
move the body to match that wire.

Mass about **25 kg**. Torque ceilings from geometry, not copied 70 kg
human numbers. `Muscle.direction`: flexor `+1`, extensor `−1`. Same
`ApplySignal` as the human: positive signal = increase `jointAngle` =
extensor.

## Sign convention (human, do not fork)

`jointAngle` = connected-body rotation minus own. The joint lives on
the child. Positive `jointAngle` rotates the child clockwise vs the
parent (distal end toward −X when facing +X).

| Joint | Flexion / role | Limit | Extensor does |
|---|---|---|---|
| Lumbar (on `Chest`) | free coupler | `−20…+20` | increases `jointAngle` |
| Neck, head | world pitch | `−30…+30` each | same |
| Jaw | open is plus (teeth down) | `0…+40` | increases `jointAngle` (opens) |
| Tail (each vertebra) | rest spring | `−40…+40` | n/a on distal; first may hold pose 0 |
| Rear hip | stance **minus** (thigh cranial; shin fold puts paw under) | `−90…+90` | increases `jointAngle` (stifle more caudal) |
| Rear knee | caudal fold, **plus** | `0…+120` | increases `jointAngle` (opens the fold) |
| Rear paw | load-bearing | `−45…+45` | CoM only, not a pose |
| Front shoulder | stance **minus** (upper cranial) | `−90…+90` | increases `jointAngle` (elbow caudal) |
| Front elbow | caudal fold, **plus** (knee analog) | `0…+120` | increases `jointAngle` |
| Front paw (carpus) | load-bearing, not a human wrist | `−45…+45` | CoM only, not a pose |

Do **not** copy `CreateArm` (`elbow −140…0`). Knee and front elbow
share the **plus** range. Hip and shoulder share `±90` limits. Quiet
stance is an inverted-V: both proximal joints **minus**, both distal
**plus** (hip −12 / shoulder −20 / knee 24 / elbow 24). Straight-leg
hip minus was the X (c39 leftover −25 / +25 / 0 / 0). Straight-leg
hip plus was the A-rake sploot (+25 / −25 / 0 / 0). Distal fold is
the new mechanism — not a return to 0/0.

## Spawn (paws on y = −2.0)

Do not use the human stacked-trunk formula
`(pelvis+torso)/2 + thigh + shin + foot`. The dog trunk is horizontal.
Front and rear soles must match:

```
H_front = (chestLocalY + shoulderInChest.y) + upper.y + forearm.y + paw.y
H_rear  = (pelvisLocalY + hipInPelvis.y) + thigh.y + shin.y + paw.y
require H_front == H_rear
y0 = -2.0 + H_front
```

If centers sit at the same Y and limbs hang straight down,
`shoulderInChest.y = −chest.y/2` and `hipInPelvis.y = −pelvis.y/2`.
A 1 cm front/rear mismatch puts two paws in the air or in the ground.
Default build pose is the standing inverted-V: `spawnHipAngle` **−12**,
`spawnShoulderAngle` **−20**, `spawnKneeAngle` **24**,
`spawnElbowAngle` **24**, matched by `hipBaseAngle` /
`shoulderBaseAngle` / `kneeBaseAngle` / `elbowBaseAngle`.
`LimbWorldAngles` is the joint→world identity
(`thighW = −hip`, `shinW = thighW − knee`,
`upperW = chestPitch − shoulder`, `lowerW = upperW − elbow`).
Hip −12 / knee 24 → thigh +12° / shin −12° (paw under the hip).
Shoulder −20 / chest −8 / elbow 24 → upper +12° / forearm −12°.
`StandingRootY` uses the same constants. Columns 0/0 lost the plant
twice (c41, c52): rear unloads ~0.15 s, lumbar slams +20. The
leftover −25 / +25 / 0 / 0 planted as a sit (`trunkDrop` 0.193)
with paws under the belly. The A-rake +25 / −25 / 0 / 0 splayed
straight legs (sploot). Do not return to 0/0 without a new mechanism.

## Control

`DogStanceController` only. Not `BalanceController`.

- Four paws: CoM vs support of **grounded** paws. Same command on all
  four: CoM ahead (+X) → positive signal → extensor. No angular PD.
  No muscle damper on paw angle. Viscosity is `JointFriction` only.
  Do not invert the front pair. Quiet stance deadzones: `pawComDeadzone`
  **0.02 m** / `pawComVelDeadzone` **0.08 m/s** (soft; 0 = old bang-bang
  that saturated at 0.83 cm), `heightDeadzone` **0.01 m**,
  `poseHoldDeadzoneDeg` **1** on hip/shoulder/knee/elbow only.
  `GetContacts` plus `IsTouching`; `pawGroundHoldSeconds` **0.03** only
  while not Walk/Leap so a missed manifold does not unload a sole.
- Rear hips / front shoulders: **joint pose** −12 / −20, not world
  pitch (c3 dropped the world loops; c8/c16 world hip lost plant).
  Distal joints hold **24 / 24** (inverted-V, paws under the trunk).
  `startupHipP` **8** for `startupHipSeconds` **0.25** holds the pose
  through the slam (DOG-2 c59). Full-time hipP 4 lost plant (c20).
  `heightP` 60: both knee and elbow **minus** lift — opening the 24°
  V lengthens the drop. Plus knee on this pose is a crouch / sploot.
  A-rake plus-knee from a −25° thigh was the previous height sign
  and sank after the hip flip. Chest / neck / head spawn: chest at
  `spawnChestPitch` **−8** (lumbar world target), neck/head/jaw at
  world **0** (SPD target). Building the neck at chest pitch was a
  second slam into the chest. Trot does not start until all four
  paws plant.
- Lumbar / chest: chest **world** pitch. Formula like human lumbar:
  `(-P)*error − (-D)*speed`. P and D stay positive. Do not PD the
  lumbar to the pelvis joint angle. Do not mix world error with
  `joint.jointSpeed`. Small plus target raises the cranial end; a
  minus target is a nose-down hold — change the target, not P.
- Front shoulders may share the chest world target **only** with the
  hip sign (`+P*error − D*speed`). Joint on the upper, chest is
  `connectedBody`. Same target + opposite formulas cooperate. The
  same formula on both loops fights.
- Rear knees / front elbows: joint pose, plus flexion.
- Neck / head: Stable PD to world (same formula as
  `ControlSegmentToWorldUpright`). Ordinary PD will chatter.
- Jaw: joint pose, closed 0. `Bark()` opens briefly and `OrganismVoice.Cry(Call)`.
  `Bite()` opens then slams shut and arms `JawStrike`. No `DogIntent`.
  Hits only from the jaw trigger, same contract as the bird beak.
- Leap attack: `LeapCrouch` → `LeapPush` → `LeapAir` → `LeapBite`.
  Coil (knee/elbow plus, hip more minus, shoulder more plus), then
  explode the fold while paws are planted, hold a stretch in the air,
  bite once. `DogDrive` or CLI calls `LeapAttack`. Headless `-dogLeap 1`
  `-dogLeapTime 2` `-dogPreyX 1.4`. Mark is `DogPrey` + `Damageable`.
  No `AddForce` / `AddTorque` for the jump: launch is knee/elbow
  extension plus `leapPawPlant` extensor on grounded paws. No paw
  angle PD. `Sense` does not classify Falling from CoM while `IsLeap()`.
- Walk: state `Walk`, clocked gait. `runSpeed` **0** is the old
  diagonal trot (FR+RL vs FL+RR, dog_w10 leftover 0.286 km/h).
  `runSpeed` **> 0** (default **1.4** m/s) is a sagittal **bound**
  (both rears, then both fronts): L/R share X, so a diagonal is a
  pitch couple (w11 dumped at extend 14). Cadence is `runStride /
  runSpeed`. Flex / extend / plant lerp from the sit-trot values
  toward `runHipFlex` / `runShoulderFlex` / `runHipExtend` /
  `runShoulderExtend` / `runKneeFlex` / `runElbowFlex` / `runPawPlant`
  at `runSpeedRef`. Chest world target is `walkChestTilt` minus
  `runChestLean` × facing (nose into the run). Four independent
  hip/shoulder/knee/elbow targets. Stance extends and
  plants (`walkPawPlant` / `runPawPlant`, rear stronger than front). Swing flexes
  then reaches, but a **grounded** swing keeps stance knee/elbow
  (folding a loaded plus-fold dumps that corner). `walkChestTilt`
  matches stance `chestTargetTilt` (−8) when `runSpeed` is 0; a jump to −4 pitched the
  pelvis. Light CoM mix on stance paws only. `Sense` does not
  `RelaxAll` from CoM during walk; fold only on real trunk drop /
  pitch. No paw angle PD. No `AddForce`. Public API is `Walk()` /
  `EndWalk()`. Quiet stand is `walkWanted` false and does not read
  `runSpeed`.
